**Issue**: #409
**Date**: 2026-09-22
**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG
**Related Spec**: specs/374-recover-bounded-automatic-delivery-stops-without-loops/

Feature: Admit a new issue after independently completed prior delivery
  A stale failed-deliver checkpoint must not block unrelated approved work once exact external delivery is proven.

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Reconcile exact delivery and retain the original failure
    Given a bound failed-deliver checkpoint for issue N with recorded pull request P and head H
    And P is merged at H with merge commit M and issue N is closed
    And M is an ancestor of the clean default checkout without an active controller or worker
    When an approved distinct issue Q is explicitly selected
    Then the original checkpoint and failed handoff remain in a durable run-identified archive
    And the normal fresh issue Q admission starts without a forged passed handoff

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Missing or contradictory external proof blocks
    Given the same failed-deliver checkpoint
    But P is open, changed head, absent, or merged at a head other than H
    Or N is open or M is not an ancestor of the current default checkout
    When issue Q is explicitly selected
    Then the old checkpoint and evidence remain unchanged and no worker starts

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Ownership and filesystem ambiguity block
    Given a missing checkpoint identity, dirty or non-default checkout, live owner, existing lock, or archive collision
    When issue Q is explicitly selected
    Then the old checkpoint and supporting evidence remain unchanged
    And no remote write or new-issue worker occurs
